<v Ira Glass>Act One. Well, the tragedy of the story of Oedipus, if you remember this from school, is that a son kills his father and marries his mother and then, of course, rips out his eyes when he realizes what it is that he's done. And the thing about this story is that he does all these things unwittingly. He doesn't know that that's what he's doing with his mother and father when he does it.
<v Ira Glass>第一幕。好吧，俄狄浦斯故事的悲剧在于，如果你还记得学校里学过的，就是一个儿子杀死了他的父亲，娶了他的母亲，然后当然，当他意识到自己做了什么时，他挖出了自己的双眼。这个故事的关键在于，他所做的一切都是在不知情的情况下发生的。当他对自己母亲和父亲做出那些事时，他并不知道自己是在做什么。

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:46.730
<v Ira Glass>Well, the first story on today's program is also about a family that ends up getting ripped apart. It's also about a family where the son ends up with the mother, the father gone. And it's also a story where the tragedy of it is that it all happens without any of them really wanting it to happen this way. It's the ending they all wanted to avoid. Nancy Updike prepared this story of an American family and of what it means to be a man.
<v Ira Glass>今天节目的第一个故事也关于一个最终分崩离析的家庭。它也关于一个儿子最终和母亲生活在一起，而父亲已经不在了。这同样是一个悲剧故事，因为这一切发生时，他们之中没有人真正希望事情变成这样。这是他们都想避免的结局。南希·厄普代克准备了这个关于美国家庭以及何谓男人的故事。

00:03:46.730 --> 00:04:06.420
<v Nancy Updike>This story is like one those Russian dolls where there's always a smaller one inside. The smallest doll, the core of the drama, is the fact that Mubarak, a childhood sissy, grew up to be a different kind of sissy than his father. His father is nerdy and bookish. Mubarak's gay.
<v Nancy Updike>这个故事就像那些俄罗斯套娃，里面总有一个更小的。最小的那个娃娃，也就是戏剧的核心，是穆巴拉克这个从小就是娘娘腔的孩子，长大后成了与他父亲不同类型的娘娘腔。他父亲是书呆子气很重的人。而穆巴拉克是同性恋。

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:17.510
<v Nancy Updike>Everything around that core gets bigger and bigger until finally you can't believe the biggest and the smallest have anything to do with each other, the one is so bloated and the other so tiny.
<v Nancy Updike>围绕着这个核心的一切变得越来越大，直到最后你无法相信最外层和最内层有什么关系，一个如此肿胀，另一个又如此渺小。

00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:37.330
<v Nancy Updike>At the beginning of this story, Mubarak's parents are married and in love, and both prepared to live far from everything they know to be with each other. At the end of the story, they may still be in love, but they're divorced and an ocean apart and not speaking. And Mubarak is caring for his mother the way a husband might.
